+Apple M1 USB4 dock display integration draft (Test125)
+====================================================
+
+Scope
+-----
+
+This downstream series captures the measured Mac mini M1 / Dynabook PS0120EA1PRP
+path: external DCP -> M1 port 1 USB4 DP-IN0 -> dock DisplayPort output.
+The transport and lifecycle code is derived from the Test125 sources. Kernel
+module dependency packaging, optional-provider stubs, default autostart, and
+board-source translation are subsequent integration changes: built and checked,
+but not yet boot-tested as a combined in-tree kernel.
+
+It is not a general multi-controller, MST, multi-monitor or suspend driver.
+The provider registry admits one selected CIO instance. The existing diagnostic
+property and function names remain deliberately visible for provenance/review.
+They are not a stable upstream binding or ABI. Full dock surprise removal and
+suspend/resume remain outside the validated scope.
+
+Source base and provenance
+--------------------------
+
+Intended repository/base: UbuntuAsahi/linux,
+f7734f4c91c0f47d9e762786968057bec99a0788
+(UBUNTU: Ubuntu-asahi-arm-7.2.0-1001.1; Linux 7.2.12).
+
+Patch reconstruction used selected paths from the original Ubuntu source
+package linux-asahi-arm-7.2 7.2.0-1001.1~26.04.1. The local repository has a
+synthetic sparse baseline, not upstream commit ancestry. The outer package
+contains source-package hashes, critical Git blob checks, the preimage manifest,
+and an application helper that requires the actual upstream base and verifies
+every affected original file before applying. A current Asahi branch is not an
+interchangeable base.
+
+Ramzi Abdiche's original EPIC notify-style reply patch is retained as a separate
+commit with its original author and Signed-off-by. The M1 clock and crossbar
+sequences reference omacom/linux-aurora at
+2f725546d6ac6afe0bd5abfa1a844971519f0076; the USB4 connection role is adapted from
+Oliver Lukschander's e37bbb4fc8f577967ea3acd8b2c27e0ce91f1138. Original reference
+metadata and licenses are retained. Our adaptations are AI-assisted and are not
+represented as endorsed or signed off by those upstream authors.
+
+Building and loading
+--------------------
+
+Use the complete pinned kernel source, its matching Ubuntu configuration and
+its compiler toolchain. Enable these existing tristates together::
+
+    CONFIG_DRM_APPLE=m
+    CONFIG_USB4=m
+    CONFIG_USB4_APPLE_SOC=m
+    CONFIG_PHY_APPLE_ATC=m
+    CONFIG_MUX_APPLE_DPXBAR=m
+
+Normal in-tree Kbuild and depmod resolve the dependencies. The source series
+contains no /run-dependent KBUILD_EXTRA_SYMBOLS paths. New shared interfaces
+live in include/linux. Built-in consumers cannot depend on modular providers;
+optional-provider stubs preserve configurations without the USB4 display path.
+Initial display routing defaults on when the explicit board route exists. The
+read-only appledrm.dpin_autostart parameter remains available for diagnosis.
+
+The J274 DT source describes the measured route with labels. Keep the primary
+DCP available for direct HDMI. The dcpext alias makes m1n1 prepare the external
+DCP; its node remains disabled until the bootloader installs firmware and
+reserved-memory properties. Never bake live firmware addresses or memory-region
+phandles into a distributed DTB. No Apple firmware or bootloader binaries are
+included in this series. The tested path used m1n1 v1.5.2 and DCP compatibility
+13.5; other firmware versions are not implied to work by this result.
+
+Compile DTs using the matching Asahi DTC. Generic distro DTC may reject existing
+floating-point GPU properties in the unmodified base sources. Build a separately
+named kernel/module set and stage its DTB via the distribution's bootloader
+packaging for a future one-shot boot. Do not mix these modules into an unrelated
+kernel or replace the current default boot entry merely to apply this series.
+
+Validated reference and pending validation
+-----------------------------------------
+
+Test125 completed standard modprobe loading at 7.924 seconds, initial display
+connection at 10.724 seconds, real DP unplug at 207.977 seconds and automatic
+reconnect at 228.940 seconds. The user confirmed stable images before and after
+hotplug. OWC reads before and after the event matched the recorded 16 MiB hash.
+The external DCP unbound at 260.111 seconds; return to stock Ubuntu was verified.
+The full final journal had no kernel panic, SError or blocked-task report.
+Known firmware PMU read errors and userspace AppArmor/service warnings remain.
+
+Earlier visual tests covered DP Video 1, DP Video 2 and HDMI Video 1. Physical
+DP hotplug in the latest reference was tested on Video 1. Do not extend this to
+HDMI Video 2, HDMI hotplug, display audio, whole-dock unplug, MST, long-duration
+stress or suspend/resume. The OWC in Test125 used the dock USB/SSD port, so that
+checksum is not a new PCIe/NVMe tunnel validation.
+
+The series was applied from scratch and the resulting tree matched the prepared
+branch. Five affected modules were built together against the matching installed
+headers, without loading them. DT route properties were compared semantically
+with the tested firmware-free DT. A full kernel build and boot of this packaged
+series remain pending. Checkpatch findings (including diagnostic formatting and
+missing local DCO sign-off) are recorded, not silently waived.
+
+Separate work
+-------------
+
+No AMDGPU, TTM, Radeon HDA, FFmpeg, NVMe, native PCIe-host, DART, CD321x or suspend
+patches are introduced by this display series. Earlier PCIe/SSD and eGPU work is
+separate. In particular, working Radeon rendering does not establish safe eGPU
+surprise removal: that path still produced SError in prior tests. Do not include
+those incomplete patches in a dock-display PR by implication.
